{"name":"Salsa Picante","hex":"#ab250b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"salsa","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A spicy tomato sauce of Mexican origin, often including onions and hot peppers.","A style of urban music originally from New York heavily influenced by Cuban dance music, jazz and rock."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To dance the salsa."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salsa"}],"entries":[{"title":"Salsa Picante","blocks":[{"text":"Salsa Picante is an album by American composer-arranger/keyboardist Clare Fischer, recorded on January 30, 1978, and marking the eponymous recording debut of Fischer's Latin jazz combo. Initially released in 1979 by MPS Records in Germany, the album's U.S. release came the following year on the Trend/Discovery label. Though long unavailable on CD, four of its tracks made it onto MPS's 1998 anthology of Fischer highlights, Latin Patterns, and the album in its entirety was finally reissued on CD in 2007 by Clare Fischer Productions."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/11/Salsa_Picante.0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salsa_Picante"},{"title":"Pace Foods","blocks":[{"text":"Pace Foods is a producer of a variety of canned salsas located in Paris, Texas. The company was founded in 1947 by David Pace when he developed a recipe for a salsa he called \"Picante sauce\", which was \"made with the freshest ingredients, harvested and hand-selected in peak season to achieve the best flavor and quality\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5f/Pace_foods_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pace_Foods"},{"title":"Salsa (food)","blocks":[{"text":"A salsa is any of a variety of sauces used as condiments for tacos and other Mexican and Mexican-American foods, and as dips for tortilla chips. They may be raw or cooked, and are generally served at room temperature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Various_salsas.jpg/330px-Various_salsas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salsa_(food)"},{"title":"Pungency","blocks":[{"text":"Pungency, commonly referred to as spiciness, hotness or heat, is a sensation that contributes to the flavor of certain foods such as chili peppers. Highly pungent foods may be experienced as unpleasant. The term piquancy is sometimes applied to foods with a lower degree of pungency that are \"agreeably stimulating to the palate\". In addition to chili peppers, piquant ingredients include wasabi, horseradish and mustard. The primary substances responsible for pungency are capsaicin, piperine and allyl isothiocyanate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/PepperswithscovilleCentralMarketHoustonTX.JPG/330px-PepperswithscovilleCentralMarketHoustonTX.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pungency"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Pace_Picante_sauce_%28Medium_salsa%29.jpg/500px-Pace_Picante_sauce_%28Medium_salsa%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Pace_Picante_sauce_%28Medium_salsa%29.jpg/1280px-Pace_Picante_sauce_%28Medium_salsa%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Pace_Picante_sauce_%28Medium_salsa%29.jpg/500px-Pace_Picante_sauce_%28Medium_salsa%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The original Picante sauce from Pace Foods has visible chunks of green bell pepper and white onion.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APace_Picante_sauce_(Medium_salsa).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg/500px-MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg/1280px-MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg/500px-MangoPineappleSalsa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Salsa made with jalapeños, mango, pineapple, red onion and cilantro (coriander)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMangoPineappleSalsa.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/AGV_4558_%2821982977281%29.jpg/500px-AGV_4558_%2821982977281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/AGV_4558_%2821982977281%29.jpg/1280px-AGV_4558_%2821982977281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/AGV_4558_%2821982977281%29.jpg/500px-AGV_4558_%2821982977281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Various types of Mexican salsas, including moles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAGV_4558_(21982977281).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Chorizo_and_egg_burrito_with_salsa.jpg/500px-Chorizo_and_egg_burrito_with_salsa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Chorizo_and_egg_burrito_with_salsa.jpg/1280px-Chorizo_and_egg_burrito_with_salsa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org